abstract: >-
  A pipeline for grading diabetic retinopathy from colour fundus photographs on the five-level ICDR scale. An image
  passes through an image-quality check, preprocessing, vessel and lesion segmentation, and an ordinal ConvNeXt-Tiny
  grader with a CORN head (three seeds, trained jointly on APTOS 2019 and EyePACS). The three-seed ensemble gives
  uncertainty scores and selective prediction; Grad-CAM, Integrated Gradients, Occlusion and superpixel SHAP explain
  the grade, and a written summary states the result and a reliability flag. The repository contains the inference,
  evaluation and training code, a local web demo and Docker image, the evaluation lists and per-image predictions that
  reproduce the reported results on the DDR and IDRiD test sets, and the manifest of the released model weights. It is a
  research prototype and not a medical device. It is the software behind a companion study of external generalisation
  of DR grading, submitted to Biomedical Signal Processing and Control.
